      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "So, tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions. I'm asking so that we don't miss anything.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:34",
      "end_timestamp": "02:42",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "I've had acid reflux for about ten years now.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:43",
      "end_timestamp": "02:48",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[0]",
        "clinical_conditions[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "I see, go ahead. Right, so acid reflux is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:50",
      "end_timestamp": "02:59",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[0]",
        "clinical_conditions[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Right, now some background about your lifestyle.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:16",
      "end_timestamp": "03:19",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.social_history[0]",
        "medical_history.social_history[1]",
        "medical_history.social_history[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_018",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit. I swim twice a week. I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:20",
      "end_timestamp": "03:31",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.social_history[0]",
        "medical_history.social_history[1]",
        "medical_history.social_history[2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Alright, do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?",
      "start_timestamp": "03:33",
      "end_timestamp": "03:37",
      "supports": [
        "medications[0]",
        "medications[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "It's something called lans... lansoprazole, 30 milligrams, maybe, before breakfast for my acidity.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:38",
      "end_timestamp": "03:45",
      "supports": [
        "medications[0]",
        "clinical_uncertainties[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Is the packet here, or the prescription?",
      "start_timestamp": "03:46",
      "end_timestamp": "03:49",
      "supports": [
        "medications[0]",
        "clinical_uncertainties[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time. Before this I was on omeprazole; that's been stopped.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:50",
      "end_timestamp": "03:59",
      "supports": [
        "medications[0]",
        "medications[1]",
        "clinical_uncertainties[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Taking everything into account, I'd lean towards trigeminal neuralgia. Another possibility is a dental problem.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:09",
      "end_timestamp": "04:16",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_assessment[0]",
        "clinical_assessment[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like trigeminal neuralgia, but I'd like to confirm. We should do an MRI scan of the head for facial pain. You'll be taking carbamazepine, 100 milligrams, twice a day, titrate. That's for nerve pain. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up. Avoid known triggers and eat soft foods when it flares. I'll also refer you to the neurology clinic.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:20",
      "end_timestamp": "04:51",
      "supports": [
        "medications[2]",
        "clinical_assessment[0]",
        "procedures_and_investigations[0]",
        "clinical_actions[0]",
        "clinical_actions[1]",
        "clinical_actions[2]",
        "clinical_actions[3]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:51",
